4> be a morphism of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0005>.\nAssume each base change <MATH_0006> has property\n<MATH_0007>. Our goal is to show that <MATH_0008> has <MATH_0009>.\nLet <MATH_0010> be an affine scheme, and let <MATH_0011> be a morphism.\nBy (2) it suffices to show that the morphism of algebraic spaces\n<MATH_0012> has <MATH_0013>.\nSince <MATH_0014> is an fpqc covering we know there\nexists a standard fpqc covering <MATH_0015>\nand morphisms <MATH_0016> over <MATH_0017> for suitable indices <MATH_0018>.\nSince <MATH_0019> has <MATH_0020> we see that\n<MATH_0021>\nhas <MATH_0022> as a base change of <MATH_0023> (see first remark of the\nproof). Set <MATH_0024>, so that <MATH_0025> is\na flat and surjective morphism of affine schemes over <MATH_0026>. By (1)\nwe conclude that <MATH_0027> has property <MATH_0028>.\nSince this is the base change of the morphism <MATH_0029>\nby the morphism <MATH_0030> we conclude that\n<MATH_0031> has property <MATH_0032> as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:90c5e8f1cb9f54b9d39ffa851cbb546def989a8f28ffec54e919d4376e20c60c", "unit_id": "tag:041J:proof"}
